<p>
Some people say there isn’t intelligence of any sort in use. I don’t know about that but I do know that AI isn’t used by Irreal in any way.
</p>
<p>
Despite my promiscuous use of em-dashes and refusal to believe that Irreal readers can’t read above the sixth grade level, every single word that appears on Irreal is written by me (except quotes, of course). The same goes for editing. My style is my own and I can’t imagine letting some program—not even a “grammar checker”—tell me to change it.
</p>
<p>
So, warts and all, there’s nobody to blame for what you see here but me. And that’s not going to change, no matter how good and capable AI gets. I suppose I could get so old and infirm that I have to dictate my posts to some speech recognition app running in Emacs but that’s not really AI. In any event, that day is not yet here so we needed worry about it.</p>
